  "live_records": {
    "q-256562": {
      "dom_id": "step-q256562",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,2]\\times [0,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{2}y-2x-{y}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,1]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">${x}_{1}=[$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n$1.25$\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y-2x-{y}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y-2x-{y}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2xy-2 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2y & 2x \\\\ 2x & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}2y & 2x \\\\ 2x & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2xy-2 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}2y & 2x \\\\ 2x & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}2xy-2 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}2(1) & 2(1) \\\\ 2(1) & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2(1)(1)-2 \\\\ (1)^{2}-2(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.25 \\\\ 0.75\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
