    "q-257190": {
      "dom_id": "step-q257190",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=3{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2}+2xy-3x.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,2]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n$0.375$\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2}+2xy-3x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2}+2xy-3x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6xy-2x+2y-3 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6xy-2x+2y-3) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}+2x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(6xy-2x+2y-3) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}+2x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6y-2 & 6x+2 \\\\ 6x+2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}6y-2 & 6x+2 \\\\ 6x+2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}6xy-2x+2y-3 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}6y-2 & 6x+2 \\\\ 6x+2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}6xy-2x+2y-3 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6(2)-2 & 6(1)+2 \\\\ 6(1)+2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}6(1)(2)-2(1)+2(2)-3 \\\\ 3(1)^{2}+2(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}10 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{10\\cdot 0-8\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{64}[\\begin{aligned}-40 \\\\ -38\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.375 \\\\ 1.406\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
