      "problem": "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,2]\\times [0,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=4{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}+xy-3{y}^{2}-2.\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,2]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}+xy-3{y}^{2}-2) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}+xy-3{y}^{2}-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8xy-4x+y \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+x-6y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8xy-4x+y) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}+x-6y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(8xy-4x+y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}+x-6y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8y-4 & 8x+1 \\\\ 8x+1 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}8y-4 & 8x+1 \\\\ 8x+1 & -6\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}8xy-4x+y \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+x-6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with\n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}8y-4 & 8x+1 \\\\ 8x+1 & -6\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}8xy-4x+y \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+x-6y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}8(2)-4 & 8(1)+1 \\\\ 8(1)+1 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}8(1)(2)-4(1)+2 \\\\ 4(1)^{2}+(1)-6(2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}12 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{12\\cdot (-6)-9\\cdot 9}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -9 \\\\ -9 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{153}[\\begin{aligned}-21 \\\\ -210\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.863 \\\\ 0.627\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
